1
00:00:02,469 --> 00:00:04,337
<i>The National Advanced Medical Care Center</i>

2
00:00:04,404 --> 00:00:07,941
<i>is full of ugly battles</i>
<i>over power and rights.</i>

3
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:11,611
<i>Totei University and Seikyo University</i>
<i>are the worst.</i>

4
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,813
I don't care which it is.

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:16,783
Let me cut him. He's my patient.

6
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:19,052
- Daimon.
- Demon.

7
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:20,820
Who's that woman?

8
00:00:20,887 --> 00:00:23,723
Heart, liver, and carotid.

9
00:00:24,691 --> 00:00:29,829
- She's doing three parts simultaneously.
- She really is a thousand-hand goddess.

10
00:00:29,896 --> 00:00:32,332
Michiko Daimon.

11
00:00:35,769 --> 00:00:39,239
From now on, please be
of use to this hospital.

12
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:41,307
I look forward to working with you.

13
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:44,811
You can do that without a medical license.

14
00:00:47,414 --> 00:00:48,515
Bye.

15
00:00:56,189 --> 00:00:59,426
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

16
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:13,573
Got it! Great!

17
00:01:22,282 --> 00:01:24,084
Which one? That one?

18
00:01:25,485 --> 00:01:28,021
Go. Yes. Yes.

19
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:28,922
Come on.

20
00:01:29,789 --> 00:01:32,792
Yes! Yes!

21
00:01:38,898 --> 00:01:41,167
Come on.

22
00:01:41,234 --> 00:01:43,303
Go.

23
00:01:43,670 --> 00:01:46,773
Yeah!

24
00:01:52,145 --> 00:01:54,581
Gosh.

25
00:01:55,882 --> 00:01:58,585
Akira, let me borrow money.

26
00:01:59,652 --> 00:02:01,688
Akira?

27
00:02:02,689 --> 00:02:03,957
Akira?

28
00:02:04,023 --> 00:02:08,761
Where are you? Where did you go?

29
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:11,264
Akira, let me borrow money.

30
00:02:11,331 --> 00:02:16,803
Michiko, this is fun, so come. Pose.

31
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:28,381
To develop medical technology that
will support the future of humanity,

32
00:02:29,015 --> 00:02:31,384
and save as many lives as possible.

33
00:02:31,451 --> 00:02:36,089
That's our mission at the National
Advanced Medical Care Center.

34
00:02:37,257 --> 00:02:41,895
This means showing to the world

35
00:02:41,961 --> 00:02:44,430
the innovativeness of
Japanese medical science.

36
00:02:45,398 --> 00:02:47,100
As a result of this,

37
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:52,272
Director Ebina of the newly founded
Strategically Integrated Surgical Dept.

38
00:02:52,872 --> 00:02:56,109
has prepared a world-class case report.

39
00:02:56,576 --> 00:03:01,014
A case of a single-stage resection
of the left atrium myxoma,

40
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:05,485
ruptured hepatocyte,
and peritoneal dissemination.

41
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:10,056
This case report will pave the way
for the future of medicine.

42
00:03:11,791 --> 00:03:16,095
I truly believe that.

43
00:03:18,398 --> 00:03:20,333
- Ebina, please.
- Yes.

44
00:03:20,934 --> 00:03:23,536
Constantly challenging
unknown territories is

45
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:28,608
the duty for us medical scientists.
There's no success without challenge.

46
00:03:29,409 --> 00:03:31,778
I hereby declare.

47
00:03:33,012 --> 00:03:35,114
"Change and challenge."

48
00:03:37,784 --> 00:03:40,053
Isn't he getting a bit too carried away?

49
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,255
Let him be.

50
00:03:43,656 --> 00:03:47,193
We won't let the east
have their way for long.

51
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:52,232
He's made a bold challenge, but
it was Dr. Daimon who did it, right?

52
00:03:52,298 --> 00:03:55,935
It doesn't matter who did it, as
long as it's credited to the east.

53
00:03:56,002 --> 00:03:59,739
Dr. Ebina, it seems like many people
missed their photo opportunity.

54
00:03:59,806 --> 00:04:02,642
- Could you strike that pose again?
- Over here, please.

55
00:04:05,878 --> 00:04:08,214
- Change and challenge.
- Over here, please.

56
00:04:10,683 --> 00:04:13,419
- Change and challenge.
- How stupid.

57
00:04:15,121 --> 00:04:16,322
Over here too.

58
00:04:17,123 --> 00:04:18,992
Change and challenge.

59
00:04:20,627 --> 00:04:21,761
You idiot.

60
00:04:21,828 --> 00:04:25,598
How many times did I tell you
not to put soy sauce on that?

61
00:04:25,665 --> 00:04:27,233
What a waste of good fish.

62
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,502
You eat this with salt and
sudachi citrus fruit?

63
00:04:34,374 --> 00:04:36,476
It's good with soy sauce too.

64
00:04:37,677 --> 00:04:41,381
Someone who doesn't understand good
sushi shouldn't come to my place.

65
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,950
The Boss' rudeness
is part of the great taste.

66
00:04:45,084 --> 00:04:45,952
Shut up.

67
00:04:48,321 --> 00:04:52,792
Should I eat it now? Should I order tuna?

68
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,195
Tuna.

69
00:05:02,735 --> 00:05:05,672
Boss, this tuna.

70
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:08,308
My son got it from a game.

71
00:05:09,242 --> 00:05:11,911
Michiko, you spent 5,000 yen
but couldn't get a single one.

72
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,146
Please don't say that.

73
00:05:13,713 --> 00:05:17,517
Don't compare yourself to my son.
Kazuya's smarter than the average kid.

74
00:05:17,583 --> 00:05:19,419
- He's a genius.
- Genius?

75
00:05:19,919 --> 00:05:25,391
He won a silver medal at the Tokyo
Mathematics Olympics or something.

76
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:26,959
He was the only grade schooler.

77
00:05:27,026 --> 00:05:30,763
Tokyo Mathematics Olympics
is where child prodigies around Tokyo

78
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:33,866
gather and compete
to solve difficult math problems?

79
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:37,870
It's like a small mullet fish
had a big tuna as a kid.

80
00:05:38,571 --> 00:05:40,773
- If you learn the trick to it.
- I want to learn it.

81
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,375
It's impossible for you.

82
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:45,712
- You were listening, huh?
- Why?

83
00:05:45,778 --> 00:05:49,382
Because you need an equation.
You wouldn't be able to solve it.

84
00:05:49,449 --> 00:05:52,785
- What sort of equation?
- I'm not telling you.

85
00:05:54,921 --> 00:05:55,988
Einstein.

86
00:05:58,257 --> 00:06:01,194
What a brat. Boss, is my tuna coming yet?

87
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:02,662
Hold on.

88
00:06:06,566 --> 00:06:07,967
My hand slipped.

89
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:16,542
- Here's your tuna.
- I've been waiting for this.

90
00:06:20,346 --> 00:06:22,915
Boss, the sushi isn't packed tightly.

91
00:06:23,816 --> 00:06:24,951
Impossible.

92
00:06:30,490 --> 00:06:31,491
Here.

93
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:36,929
- Michiko, that's bad manners.
- It's not my fault.

94
00:06:57,850 --> 00:06:59,552
Director of the surgical department,

95
00:06:59,619 --> 00:07:02,088
- you forgot this.
- Thank you.

96
00:07:05,291 --> 00:07:07,527
Strategically Integrated
Surgical Dept. Director.

97
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:09,829
Sounds nice.

98
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:13,032
DIRECTOR'S OFFICE
STRATEGICALLY INTEGRATED SURGICAL DEPT

99
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,209
Good morning, Director Ebina.

100
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:24,410
Hello.

101
00:07:25,344 --> 00:07:26,479
Who are you?

102
00:07:26,546 --> 00:07:30,483
I'm Tomoko Sekigahara,
your secretary starting today.

103
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:35,888
- My secretary?
- Yes. I'll do my best.

104
00:07:36,422 --> 00:07:37,990
Let me know if you need anything.

105
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:48,134
Your best. Anything.

106
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:52,805
- Yes?
- Hi.

107
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,809
- Thanks for coming.
- Thank you for having me.

108
00:07:59,712 --> 00:08:01,314
Why are there two doors?

109
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:04,283
I guess one of the doors is for my room.

110
00:08:04,350 --> 00:08:05,585
Dr. Dangozaka.

111
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:07,220
I've been appointed as the

112
00:08:07,286 --> 00:08:10,756
Strategically Integrated Surgical
Department Director as well.

113
00:08:11,257 --> 00:08:15,561
- I'm Dangozaka.
- I'm Sekigahara. Nice to meet you.

114
00:08:15,628 --> 00:08:16,863
Nice to meet you too.

115
00:08:16,929 --> 00:08:20,833
- Sekigahara. That's a nice name.
- Thank you.

116
00:08:21,567 --> 00:08:25,905
President Tendo is going to
have us compete until the very end.

117
00:08:26,372 --> 00:08:31,544
But isn't he wishing for
the east and west to work together?

118
00:08:31,611 --> 00:08:35,181
It means his official stance
and true intentions are different.

119
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:40,186
Who knows what he's really thinking?

120
00:08:42,221 --> 00:08:48,861
I guess there's no other choice
but to fight until one of us dies.

121
00:08:49,862 --> 00:08:53,165
I accept your challenge.
But the outcome is already clear.

122
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,167
Well thank you.

123
00:08:56,168 --> 00:08:57,003
Excuse me.

124
00:08:58,971 --> 00:09:01,941
Would you scan your
fingerprints for identification?

125
00:09:03,175 --> 00:09:04,377
How high-tech.

126
00:09:10,816 --> 00:09:11,717
I've confirmed.

127
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,253
Please.

128
00:09:19,792 --> 00:09:23,396
- Confirmed.
- I'll go in here.

129
00:09:24,163 --> 00:09:25,064
Alright.

130
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:27,934
It's so narrow.

131
00:09:30,703 --> 00:09:31,537
It's far.

132
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:36,909
Please use the rooms however you'd like.

133
00:09:45,985 --> 00:09:47,320
So small.

134
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:57,563
Strategic?

135
00:10:01,734 --> 00:10:02,802
Why integration?

136
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:23,189
- I'll draw a boundary line here.
- Boundary line?

137
00:10:23,689 --> 00:10:28,828
It's ridiculous to have
the east and west in one place.

138
00:10:28,894 --> 00:10:29,862
My eyes hurt.

139
00:10:31,564 --> 00:10:33,699
If we don't split up,
I won't be able to work.

140
00:10:34,834 --> 00:10:38,804
Dr. Futaba, you've been
poisoned by the system too.

141
00:10:38,871 --> 00:10:41,507
I haven't been poisoned by money like you.

142
00:10:42,608 --> 00:10:46,445
Kaji of the east and Futaba
of the west. I miss those days.

143
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:51,817
You mean Futaba of the west
and Kaji of the east. I come first.

144
00:10:51,884 --> 00:10:53,886
- There were days like that?
- I don't know.

145
00:10:55,688 --> 00:10:57,123
How is this?

146
00:10:59,425 --> 00:11:03,396
It's fine. We'll be using this side.

147
00:11:03,729 --> 00:11:09,635
Fine. So this is the fateful line
that separates all?

148
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,672
That's right.

149
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:20,813
The Strategically Integrated
Surgical Department Directors

150
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,782
will be making the rounds.

151
00:11:24,950 --> 00:11:27,787
The Strategically Integrated
Surgical Department Directors

152
00:11:28,154 --> 00:11:29,855
will be making the rounds.

153
00:11:35,728 --> 00:11:40,266
<i>In 2014, medical establishments</i>
<i>collapsed and became more corrupt.</i>

154
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:44,670
<i>The field of medicine,</i>
<i>which deals with people's lives,</i>

155
00:11:44,737 --> 00:11:47,273
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

156
00:11:59,618 --> 00:12:05,391
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>
<i>Japan announced to export</i>

157
00:12:05,458 --> 00:12:10,029
<i>state of the art medical services</i>
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

158
00:12:10,096 --> 00:12:14,400
<i>The world of medicine entered another era</i>
<i>following the law of jungle.</i>

159
00:12:20,139 --> 00:12:22,875
Thank you for coming, Professor Kazama.

160
00:12:23,542 --> 00:12:27,046
I know I came on short notice,
but thank you,

161
00:12:27,113 --> 00:12:29,281
- Dr. Tendo.
- Please don't worry.

162
00:12:29,849 --> 00:12:33,319
We'll provide you with
the world's best medical care.

163
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:03,783
<i>Doctors who don't belong to</i>
<i>any medical offices appeared.</i>

164
00:13:03,849 --> 00:13:07,286
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>maverick doctors.</i>

165
00:13:08,354 --> 00:13:10,156
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

166
00:13:10,823 --> 00:13:14,426
<i>She despises teams, authority</i>
<i>and the restraints they bring.</i>

167
00:13:14,493 --> 00:13:19,231
<i>Her license and the skills</i>
<i>she has earned are her only weapons.</i>

168
00:13:19,298 --> 00:13:22,601
- Daimon, don't walk in front of us.
- Move out of the way.

169
00:13:22,668 --> 00:13:23,669
Daimon.

170
00:13:23,736 --> 00:13:25,905
I won't do that.

171
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:32,945
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

172
00:14:35,975 --> 00:14:39,645
- Have you been well?
- Yes. Good morning.

173
00:14:40,279 --> 00:14:41,847
Good morning.

174
00:14:47,419 --> 00:14:50,522
PREOPERATIVE CONFERENCE

175
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:04,870
- Daimon.
- I won't do that.

176
00:15:06,772 --> 00:15:08,407
Good morning, everyone.

177
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:10,910
Good morning.

178
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:16,315
We'll now begin
this week's preoperative conference.

179
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:20,185
The first case is Shoji Kazama,
a 35-year-old male.

180
00:15:20,653 --> 00:15:24,323
The preoperative diagnosis is
craniopharyngioma, a brain tumor.

181
00:15:25,491 --> 00:15:27,593
Shoji Kazama? The physicist?

182
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:31,330
Prof. Kazama is a professor at
Harvard Institute of Technology,

183
00:15:31,397 --> 00:15:35,601
and is said to be the one closest
to winning the Nobel Prize in Japan.

184
00:15:36,468 --> 00:15:41,006
It's not an overstatement to say
his brain is a treasure of Japan.

185
00:15:41,707 --> 00:15:43,742
A tumor has formed in this brain.

186
00:15:44,476 --> 00:15:46,211
This is a national emergency.

187
00:15:46,979 --> 00:15:50,282
Losing him would be a big loss for Japan.

188
00:15:50,349 --> 00:15:56,088
- Please do not forget this fact.
- Yes, sir.

189
00:15:57,323 --> 00:16:01,193
Huh? They should
integrate their pronunciation.

190
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:04,563
The tumor is located in
the third ventricle of the brain,

191
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:07,399
and it's beyond the stage
where it can be removed nasally.

192
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:12,871
We plan to perform this surgery
using the surgical robot EX-5.

193
00:16:12,938 --> 00:16:14,573
EX-5?

194
00:16:15,407 --> 00:16:17,609
This is the surgical robot EX-5

195
00:16:17,676 --> 00:16:19,812
that is being clinically researched here.

196
00:16:20,412 --> 00:16:23,549
While monitoring the brain with
images from an endoscopic camera,

197
00:16:23,615 --> 00:16:28,020
the robot arm can be moved 40 times
more precisely than a doctor's hand.

198
00:16:29,188 --> 00:16:31,557
Furthermore, the incision
in the brain is small.

199
00:16:31,623 --> 00:16:34,159
The patient can be discharged
after 4 days.

200
00:16:36,729 --> 00:16:40,299
Complete removal of a brain tumor
using a surgical robot

201
00:16:40,366 --> 00:16:41,734
is a first case in the world.

202
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:47,306
Please show the world a speedy
and brilliant case report.

203
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:52,978
- Yes, sir.
- I said different accents.

204
00:16:53,045 --> 00:16:54,646
The doctor in charge will be...

205
00:16:54,713 --> 00:16:59,151
I believe Dr. Futaba
of the west would be perfect.

206
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:00,753
Me?

207
00:17:00,819 --> 00:17:05,724
When Dr. Futaba worked at Seikyo
University's Kyobashi Hospital,

208
00:17:05,791 --> 00:17:09,661
he had experience using the EX-5.

209
00:17:10,429 --> 00:17:13,399
Dr. Kaji, we don't have
a brain surgery specialist?

210
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:16,068
- No.
- I see.

211
00:17:18,704 --> 00:17:21,974
Then Dr. Futaba, I'll let you handle this.

212
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:25,544
Thank you, sir.

213
00:17:28,514 --> 00:17:33,085
The time has finally come
to show the world your skills.

214
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:34,987
Yes, sir.

215
00:17:38,791 --> 00:17:42,728
- Dr. Ebina, it's up.
- What is?

216
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:44,963
Daimon's hand.

217
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,269
What is it, Daimon?

218
00:17:52,671 --> 00:17:53,505
I'll do it.

219
00:17:56,308 --> 00:18:00,512
- You'll use the EX-5?
- I won't do that.

220
00:18:03,148 --> 00:18:07,719
My hand is much more perfect
and accurate than a robot.

221
00:18:07,786 --> 00:18:08,821
She declared it.

222
00:18:09,855 --> 00:18:12,758
Dr. Daimon seems to think of
Japan's most brilliant brain

223
00:18:12,825 --> 00:18:14,426
as material for experiment.

224
00:18:14,827 --> 00:18:17,696
- This is ridiculous.
- Daimon, behave yourself.

225
00:18:18,163 --> 00:18:20,232
- Why?
- Dr. Michiko Daimon.

226
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:29,875
It seems you lack some respect
for something called technology.

227
00:18:30,642 --> 00:18:33,879
- I'm sorry. Get her out of here.
- Yes, sir.

228
00:18:36,048 --> 00:18:38,250
- Get out.
- Hold on.

229
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:49,027
Dr. Daimon.
I'll have you be the assistant.

230
00:18:49,728 --> 00:18:50,562
Assistant?

231
00:18:51,897 --> 00:18:55,334
Please see how great the most
advanced surgical robot is,

232
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:58,637
and make good use of it in your career.

233
00:19:02,608 --> 00:19:04,343
An assistant, huh?

234
00:19:32,538 --> 00:19:33,906
What is this?

235
00:19:35,073 --> 00:19:35,941
I'm sorry.

236
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:39,411
I was calculating the coherence of light.

237
00:19:40,812 --> 00:19:45,083
I'm sorry to bother you
while you're working.

238
00:19:45,150 --> 00:19:45,984
It's fine.

239
00:19:46,385 --> 00:19:49,054
I'm Dangozaka, the director of

240
00:19:49,121 --> 00:19:51,223
the Strategically Integrated
Surgical Dept.

241
00:19:51,290 --> 00:19:55,594
- He's the surgeon...
- I don't need an informed consent.

242
00:19:56,728 --> 00:20:00,132
I understand there's
risk involved in surgery.

243
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:05,170
In physics research,
over 99% are failures.

244
00:20:05,837 --> 00:20:09,575
You can say that it's
a battle against infinite failure.

245
00:20:12,611 --> 00:20:18,116
Humanity cannot make progress
if they're afraid of risks.

246
00:20:21,153 --> 00:20:28,126
Failures are important experiences
which give us new tasks and paths.

247
00:20:28,193 --> 00:20:29,795
I don't mean to sound rude,

248
00:20:30,362 --> 00:20:35,067
but do you think that we're
going to fail your surgery?

249
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:38,203
Of course not.

250
00:20:39,338 --> 00:20:46,311
As a result of one life being lost,
it paves the way to the future.

251
00:20:46,378 --> 00:20:48,547
That's what progress is.

252
00:20:49,481 --> 00:20:53,418
However, losing my life is the same
as ruining the future of mankind

253
00:20:53,852 --> 00:21:00,092
that would've made
great progress with my work.

254
00:21:00,993 --> 00:21:04,696
Please decide
what's important for humanity.

255
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:06,865
I understand.

256
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:09,668
I'm the surgeon, Futaba.

257
00:21:10,369 --> 00:21:14,339
I'll do my best for your surgery,
so please rest assured.

258
00:21:14,406 --> 00:21:17,809
I heard about the EX-5
from President Tendo.

259
00:21:18,677 --> 00:21:23,282
My brain will be saved using
the finest medical technology.

260
00:21:23,749 --> 00:21:25,350
It's quite wonderful.

261
00:21:26,485 --> 00:21:27,753
Thank you.

262
00:21:29,554 --> 00:21:30,989
Please leave it to us.

263
00:21:31,056 --> 00:21:32,958
For humanity's future.

264
00:21:35,727 --> 00:21:37,829
For humanity's future.

265
00:21:37,896 --> 00:21:39,498
For humanity's future.

266
00:21:40,666 --> 00:21:43,468
- For humanity's future...
- I won't do that.

267
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:47,639
I won't do things you can do
without a medical license.

268
00:21:48,674 --> 00:21:49,641
Besides.

269
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:53,545
In the end, you just don't want to die.

270
00:21:54,079 --> 00:21:55,013
Daimon.

271
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:59,985
- Who are you?
- I'm Daimon, the assistant. Bye.

272
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:05,691
I'm terribly sorry.
We'll get another assistant right away.

273
00:22:26,244 --> 00:22:28,313
It's freshly made. It's hot.

274
00:22:28,380 --> 00:22:30,782
It's hot.

275
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:34,453
How can guys of the west eat white rice
with "okonomiyaki" pancakes?

276
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:36,355
There's takoyaki too.

277
00:22:36,421 --> 00:22:38,190
It's sort of pitiful.

278
00:22:39,491 --> 00:22:42,627
You got a lovely lunch made by
your wife as usual? It looks good.

279
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:44,296
Love must be

280
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:46,698
- accumulated every day.
- Whatever.

281
00:22:46,765 --> 00:22:48,734
Demon, you're not eating?

282
00:22:49,267 --> 00:22:50,769
Aren't I great?

283
00:22:50,836 --> 00:22:54,106
- Hi.
- Boss, over here.

284
00:22:55,774 --> 00:22:59,611
This is really special.
We don't do delivery.

285
00:23:00,579 --> 00:23:01,713
Sushi?

286
00:23:02,647 --> 00:23:05,217
- Thanks. Here you go.
- Just one coin?

287
00:23:05,283 --> 00:23:07,953
I've been waiting for this.

288
00:23:10,155 --> 00:23:11,623
Tuna, tuna, and ginger.

289
00:23:12,023 --> 00:23:15,160
- I'd say tuna, ginger, and tuna.
- Whatever.

290
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:17,929
Return the bowl on your
way home or something.

291
00:23:19,331 --> 00:23:20,265
Wait.

292
00:23:27,639 --> 00:23:30,842
It's not packed tightly.
You didn't do a good job again.

293
00:23:32,177 --> 00:23:35,647
What are you talking about?
Stop acting like you know.

294
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:39,184
Boss.

295
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:42,554
Do your hands and feet feel weak?

296
00:23:44,322 --> 00:23:45,891
It's not a big deal.

297
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:50,495
- Someone get a stretcher.
- Yes.

298
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:10,148
- There's a tumor in the midbrain.
- A brain stem glioma.

299
00:24:10,215 --> 00:24:12,284
Intraparenchymal tumor of the brain stem.

300
00:24:13,218 --> 00:24:16,555
- It's worse than Prof. Kazama.
- We have to operate now.

301
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:18,089
It's not in such a condition.

302
00:24:19,057 --> 00:24:23,061
Removing the tumor will damage
the brain stem no matter what.

303
00:24:24,429 --> 00:24:27,432
This is clearly inoperable.

304
00:24:36,174 --> 00:24:38,076
Is something wrong with me?

305
00:24:39,978 --> 00:24:43,815
You have to be hospitalized,
and you need surgery.

306
00:24:45,650 --> 00:24:48,587
You must be kidding me.
I don't have time for that.

307
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:49,488
Boss.

308
00:24:50,255 --> 00:24:53,425
I'm going to go home and make sushi.

309
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:57,128
- Forget the stupid hospital.
- Even if you go, you can't make sushi.

310
00:24:58,463 --> 00:25:01,800
There's a tumor in your brain.

311
00:25:06,204 --> 00:25:09,708
At your restaurant, I listen to
what you say, but this is hospital.

312
00:25:10,375 --> 00:25:12,344
Listen to what I say.

313
00:25:16,248 --> 00:25:19,851
- Dad.
- Kazuya. Why are you here?

314
00:25:19,918 --> 00:25:21,720
I heard that you collapsed.

315
00:25:22,854 --> 00:25:24,256
I told him.

316
00:25:26,057 --> 00:25:27,893
How nosy of you.

317
00:25:28,460 --> 00:25:29,427
Are you alright?

318
00:25:29,928 --> 00:25:32,864
It's not a big deal.

319
00:25:33,732 --> 00:25:38,603
They'll let me go if I lay down for
a while, so wait outside, alright?

320
00:25:45,944 --> 00:25:46,811
Alright.

321
00:25:57,155 --> 00:25:58,690
Am I going to die?

322
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:04,796
In your current condition, yes.

323
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:10,435
I want to see Kazuya grow up.

324
00:26:11,703 --> 00:26:15,273
He's certainly going to
become a great man.

325
00:26:17,275 --> 00:26:18,777
I want to see that.

326
00:26:23,882 --> 00:26:26,885
So you'll listen to what I tell you?

327
00:26:29,087 --> 00:26:32,657
I don't put soy sauce
on fish that calls for sudachi.

328
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:39,464
So stubborn. Here, use this.

329
00:26:44,035 --> 00:26:48,239
If the west uses EX-5 and
the operation succeeds,

330
00:26:48,306 --> 00:26:50,041
it'll be the first case in the world.

331
00:26:54,713 --> 00:26:55,714
Don't be disappointed.

332
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:57,983
But at this rate,

333
00:26:58,883 --> 00:27:02,387
our lead that we gained from
Dr. Busujima's surgery will be lost.

334
00:27:03,555 --> 00:27:07,325
No, they might even take the lead.

335
00:27:08,059 --> 00:27:10,895
"The first" is what's important.

336
00:27:10,962 --> 00:27:11,796
Yeah.

337
00:27:13,565 --> 00:27:19,504
Isn't there something
that would let us win?

338
00:27:21,473 --> 00:27:23,341
How about thinking of it this way?

339
00:27:26,344 --> 00:27:27,412
So you have something?

340
00:27:29,347 --> 00:27:31,282
- Yes.
- What is it?

341
00:27:35,286 --> 00:27:39,958
A world's first means that there
hasn't been any case of success.

342
00:27:40,525 --> 00:27:45,964
Doesn't that mean that there'll be
a higher chance of failure for this case?

343
00:27:47,565 --> 00:27:48,400
You're right.

344
00:27:49,134 --> 00:27:53,271
Let's be confident. That we can win.

345
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:56,641
Change and...

346
00:27:57,809 --> 00:27:59,077
- "Challenge."
- Yes.

347
00:28:07,285 --> 00:28:11,122
- This is just between you and me.
- Yes.

348
00:28:12,457 --> 00:28:13,925
I know.

349
00:28:16,061 --> 00:28:18,630
You've killed a man before, right?

350
00:28:23,468 --> 00:28:25,437
With a robot, right?

351
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:29,240
Murder? Robot?

352
00:28:31,342 --> 00:28:33,878
The patient died a moth after the surgery.

353
00:28:33,945 --> 00:28:36,214
It's not clear
if the surgery caused it either.

354
00:28:36,281 --> 00:28:38,049
The hospital won't make it clear.

355
00:28:40,585 --> 00:28:43,455
They can't say you killed him.

356
00:28:44,355 --> 00:28:46,357
This was 10 years ago.

357
00:28:47,192 --> 00:28:50,729
I'm much better than those days.
Please leave it to me.

358
00:28:52,630 --> 00:28:54,566
You're quite confident.

359
00:28:55,033 --> 00:28:56,134
But this time,

360
00:28:57,802 --> 00:29:01,906
you can't let the patient die.

361
00:29:01,973 --> 00:29:06,678
If you do, it'll be
much worse than us getting fired.

362
00:29:07,879 --> 00:29:08,713
I understand.

363
00:29:17,522 --> 00:29:20,959
- I'm counting on you.
- Yes, sir.

364
00:29:21,025 --> 00:29:27,432
<i>You're the very last woman...</i>

365
00:29:58,797 --> 00:29:59,631
Hello.

366
00:30:01,766 --> 00:30:02,600
Oh, it's you.

367
00:30:04,369 --> 00:30:08,039
If you want to become the assistant
again, talking to me is useless.

368
00:30:08,439 --> 00:30:09,474
That's not it.

369
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:11,676
Then what is it?

370
00:30:13,511 --> 00:30:16,614
Would you take a picture?

371
00:30:18,616 --> 00:30:19,484
With me?

372
00:30:20,919 --> 00:30:24,756
Such a big fan. Since a little kid.

373
00:30:26,090 --> 00:30:29,160
Then you should've said so from
the start instead of being so rude.

374
00:30:29,861 --> 00:30:30,728
Come in.

375
00:30:32,764 --> 00:30:34,599
- He said yes.
- Really?

376
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:39,838
It's the BSD conjecture.

377
00:30:40,805 --> 00:30:43,208
You know this equation?

378
00:30:43,274 --> 00:30:47,846
I won the silver medal at the Tokyo
Mathematics Olympics this year.

379
00:30:48,213 --> 00:30:50,048
The Tokyo Mathematics Olympics?

380
00:30:50,548 --> 00:30:55,086
Yes. No on in the world
has solved this equation, right?

381
00:30:55,687 --> 00:30:56,988
I'll solve it one day.

382
00:30:57,755 --> 00:30:59,724
It won't take long. Tomorrow.

383
00:31:00,291 --> 00:31:01,125
Amazing.

384
00:31:01,192 --> 00:31:04,195
- You said the silver medal, right?
- Yes.

385
00:31:04,262 --> 00:31:07,899
The silver medal is 2nd place.
2nd place is meaningless.

386
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,402
In the world of mathematics and physics,

387
00:31:11,736 --> 00:31:15,106
anything besides 1st place
is the same as last place.

388
00:31:16,140 --> 00:31:20,011
If you're 2nd place at the Tokyo
Mathematics Olympics,

389
00:31:20,078 --> 00:31:23,815
you're not good at all.
You won't be promised a bright future.

390
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:27,151
Who wants to be promised such a future?

391
00:31:27,218 --> 00:31:30,221
However, there's slight hope.

392
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,992
When I joined
the Tokyo Mathematics Olympics

393
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:37,795
for the first time in middle school,
I won the bronze medal.

394
00:31:38,830 --> 00:31:40,732
That means I was in the 3rd place.

395
00:31:42,367 --> 00:31:44,168
That's where it all started for me.

396
00:31:45,203 --> 00:31:47,272
I worked my way up from there.

397
00:31:48,473 --> 00:31:49,741
You're still in grade school,

398
00:31:50,408 --> 00:31:52,944
but you're already
a step above where I started.

399
00:31:53,945 --> 00:31:55,680
Don't stop trying.

400
00:31:56,581 --> 00:31:57,415
Yes.

401
00:31:57,982 --> 00:32:00,985
Alright, let's take a picture together.

402
00:32:01,052 --> 00:32:05,223
You, the assistant that was fired.
Will you take it for us?

403
00:32:05,823 --> 00:32:06,991
I'm Daimon.

404
00:32:08,092 --> 00:32:09,160
Take a good picture.

405
00:32:11,329 --> 00:32:12,797
I'll do my best.

406
00:32:18,069 --> 00:32:20,672
You can do this without a medical license.

407
00:32:20,738 --> 00:32:22,407
Say cheese.

408
00:32:32,717 --> 00:32:36,287
Prof. Kazama is amazing. He's cool too.

409
00:32:37,855 --> 00:32:38,823
Really?

410
00:32:39,390 --> 00:32:42,927
I'm going to become the world's
best physicist like Prof. Kazama.

411
00:32:43,728 --> 00:32:46,998
I think your dad's a greater man.

412
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:52,170
My dad's just a sushi chef.
He's not great at all.

413
00:32:53,171 --> 00:32:54,072
Eat that.

414
00:32:55,039 --> 00:32:57,575
I'm tired of sushi to tell you the truth.

415
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:58,676
Just eat it.

416
00:33:06,484 --> 00:33:07,318
What is this?

417
00:33:08,586 --> 00:33:11,589
It's totally different
from your dad's sushi, right?

418
00:33:13,091 --> 00:33:19,330
The sushi your dad makes is hard on
the outside, but soft on the inside.

419
00:33:19,397 --> 00:33:21,165
That's why it's good.

420
00:33:22,567 --> 00:33:26,604
Look all over the world, but your
dad is the only one who can do that.

421
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:27,505
Really?

422
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:34,145
Your dad's sushi is No. 1 in the world.

423
00:33:35,613 --> 00:33:39,851
- My dad is No. 1 in the world?
- Amazing.

424
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:48,559
See? It's completely different.

425
00:33:49,827 --> 00:33:50,661
Pon.

426
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:56,000
- You sure do play aggressively today.
- Maybe she's angry that she was fired

427
00:33:56,067 --> 00:33:58,302
from being the assistant
in Prof. Kazama's surgery.

428
00:34:00,605 --> 00:34:01,506
Pon.

429
00:34:03,074 --> 00:34:04,242
She did it again.

430
00:34:04,876 --> 00:34:07,645
I put in Hiromi instead
for Prof. Kazama's surgery.

431
00:34:08,279 --> 00:34:09,247
Me?

432
00:34:09,313 --> 00:34:12,216
It's ridiculous to have Michiko as
an assistant and fire right away.

433
00:34:12,283 --> 00:34:15,086
This is business for us too,
so I forced you in there.

434
00:34:15,153 --> 00:34:19,457
Must be exciting to be in the surgery room
with one of the most brilliant minds.

435
00:34:19,524 --> 00:34:21,592
I mean, you like brand name things.

436
00:34:22,393 --> 00:34:27,298
- Pon.
- What? You make me so mad.

437
00:34:27,365 --> 00:34:31,102
- Make sure to get paid well.
- I know.

438
00:34:31,169 --> 00:34:33,538
I don't care about
the world's brightest mind,

439
00:34:33,604 --> 00:34:36,908
but Michiko, are you really
going to do the other operation?

440
00:34:36,974 --> 00:34:38,810
Intraparenchymal tumor in the midbrain.

441
00:34:38,876 --> 00:34:41,212
The most you can cut is 5mm.
How long will it take?

442
00:34:41,279 --> 00:34:43,047
It doesn't matter how long.

443
00:34:43,114 --> 00:34:45,917
I'm sorry for the Boss,
but you can't do that operation.

444
00:34:45,983 --> 00:34:48,453
- Why?
- The tumor's in the worst spot.

445
00:34:48,519 --> 00:34:52,056
I agree. No one in
this world can perform surgery

446
00:34:52,123 --> 00:34:54,125
with such precise movements.

447
00:34:54,192 --> 00:34:56,461
Radiation is usually required for
tumors in that area.

448
00:34:56,527 --> 00:34:58,062
And see how things go, right?

449
00:34:58,129 --> 00:35:02,400
But if I don't cut him, you won't be
able to eat his tuna sushi anymore.

450
00:35:03,034 --> 00:35:06,270
- So you take tuna over humanity's future?
- That's right.

451
00:35:07,238 --> 00:35:11,242
I know you don't have this tile.
Take this.

452
00:35:11,309 --> 00:35:13,077
Pon.

453
00:35:17,648 --> 00:35:19,183
That's "Big Dragons."

454
00:35:20,918 --> 00:35:24,088
Come on.

455
00:35:25,423 --> 00:35:29,160
- That's it.
- Ron.

456
00:35:29,660 --> 00:35:31,662
I win.

457
00:35:31,729 --> 00:35:35,199
Yes!

458
00:35:35,266 --> 00:35:36,234
I'm done.

459
00:35:37,435 --> 00:35:40,505
You were really able to
draw it on such a small thing?

460
00:35:40,571 --> 00:35:46,344
- Yeah, I drew Akira.
- My face? Let me see.

461
00:35:51,349 --> 00:35:55,653
What? Let me see.

462
00:35:57,955 --> 00:36:01,592
- Goodness.
- That's great, Mai.

463
00:36:01,659 --> 00:36:05,029
- I have you too, Michiko.
- Really?

464
00:36:08,566 --> 00:36:10,234
I WON'T DO THAT

465
00:36:11,435 --> 00:36:16,741
- I want your hands, Mai.
- It says "I won't do that."

466
00:36:44,969 --> 00:36:50,675
We'll now begin third ventricle
tumor removal surgery with the EX-5.

467
00:36:51,242 --> 00:36:54,545
- Let's begin.
- Yes.

468
00:36:55,279 --> 00:36:59,116
Vitals. Blood pressure in the 100s.
Pulse in the 60s and sinus.

469
00:36:59,450 --> 00:37:03,454
Another world's first case
will come about from our hospital.

470
00:37:03,521 --> 00:37:04,689
It's quite wonderful.

471
00:37:05,122 --> 00:37:10,494
You guys don't have a talented brain
surgeon like him, do you?

472
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:15,600
The east is a little behind. In the head.

473
00:37:16,334 --> 00:37:22,473
President Tendo, Futaba
will succeed. Rest assured.

474
00:37:48,466 --> 00:37:50,067
Entering the foramen of Monro.

475
00:37:50,134 --> 00:37:52,303
ICP is under 20 and stable.

476
00:38:07,018 --> 00:38:08,386
So detailed.

477
00:38:12,890 --> 00:38:13,891
I can't do this.

478
00:38:14,892 --> 00:38:16,193
So tired.

479
00:38:21,832 --> 00:38:23,434
- Yes?
- Daimon.

480
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:30,274
Excuse me.

481
00:38:30,341 --> 00:38:32,376
Mr. Tsukiji, hang in there.
You'll be alright.

482
00:38:32,443 --> 00:38:33,978
My head hurts.

483
00:38:34,045 --> 00:38:35,179
- Hurry.
- Excuse me.

484
00:38:35,246 --> 00:38:37,782
You're going to be fine.

485
00:38:48,526 --> 00:38:49,560
It's going to sting.

486
00:38:52,596 --> 00:38:54,365
Mr. Tsukiji, you're alright.

487
00:39:00,671 --> 00:39:05,076
Possibility of acute hydrocephalus.
Get a CT right away. Prepare for drainage.

488
00:39:05,810 --> 00:39:07,645
- You're really going to do it?
- Help me.

489
00:39:08,412 --> 00:39:09,347
Don't order me.

490
00:39:09,413 --> 00:39:10,748
- Here.
- Yes.

491
00:39:11,248 --> 00:39:14,318
Tumor confirmed.
I'll separate the membrane.

492
00:39:28,299 --> 00:39:29,400
The bleeding won't stop.

493
00:39:34,472 --> 00:39:38,943
Dr. Futaba? What happened?

494
00:39:39,810 --> 00:39:42,380
- I've damaged the choroidal artery.
- What?

495
00:39:44,081 --> 00:39:47,918
My goodness. This is bad.

496
00:39:56,761 --> 00:39:58,062
The bleeding won't stop.

497
00:40:02,266 --> 00:40:06,604
What's wrong, Dr. Futaba? What happened?

498
00:40:07,505 --> 00:40:10,040
- I've damaged the choroidal artery.
- What?

499
00:40:11,275 --> 00:40:15,446
My goodness. This is bad.

500
00:40:16,647 --> 00:40:18,516
I'm leaving for a bit.

501
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:24,588
Kaji, things are turning in our favor.

502
00:40:24,655 --> 00:40:26,557
Now's not the time.

503
00:40:28,459 --> 00:40:30,995
- It's an emergency over here.
- What?

504
00:40:33,931 --> 00:40:37,301
The Demon's about to operate
on an inoperable patient.

505
00:40:37,368 --> 00:40:39,904
You must be kidding me.
Stop her immediately.

506
00:40:39,970 --> 00:40:44,508
You think she'll stop if I tell her to?
Please make her stop. Don't be stupid.

507
00:40:47,578 --> 00:40:48,412
What should I do?

508
00:40:50,681 --> 00:40:51,649
What should I do?

509
00:40:52,716 --> 00:40:53,551
How is it?

510
00:40:54,418 --> 00:40:56,720
The cerebral edema
around the tumor is advanced.

511
00:40:57,221 --> 00:40:58,622
Stop the drainage.

512
00:40:59,423 --> 00:41:02,126
Switching to tumor removal.
Subtemporal approach.

513
00:41:02,193 --> 00:41:03,260
That's reckless.

514
00:41:03,327 --> 00:41:06,397
- Get ready immediately.
- Yes.

515
00:41:08,499 --> 00:41:10,968
Oh no. I don't know
where the blood's coming from.

516
00:41:11,602 --> 00:41:13,003
What should I do?

517
00:41:15,940 --> 00:41:18,642
Blood pressure dropping. 50s. Pulse 120.

518
00:41:19,043 --> 00:41:21,479
Admission of infusion.
Beginning blood transfusion.

519
00:41:21,545 --> 00:41:22,746
Please confirm.

520
00:41:23,547 --> 00:41:24,482
It's over.

521
00:41:25,416 --> 00:41:28,452
If we kill the world's greatest
mind, this hospital is finished.

522
00:41:29,453 --> 00:41:30,221
What do I do?

523
00:41:30,287 --> 00:41:32,356
Isn't there anything
we can do, Dr. Dangozaka?

524
00:41:33,257 --> 00:41:35,426
- You're the director, right?
- What do we do?

525
00:41:36,393 --> 00:41:38,696
Futaba, do it.

526
00:41:39,330 --> 00:41:40,998
Failure is not an option.

527
00:41:42,433 --> 00:41:43,267
President Tendo.

528
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:48,038
Please call Dr. Daimon.

529
00:41:50,140 --> 00:41:51,742
What are you saying, President?

530
00:41:53,577 --> 00:41:55,312
Daimon is doing a different surgery.

531
00:41:55,379 --> 00:41:56,647
Bring her.

532
00:41:58,415 --> 00:41:59,250
Yes, sir.

533
00:42:00,851 --> 00:42:01,719
Here I go, Boss.

534
00:42:02,586 --> 00:42:04,188
Begin brain stem glioma removal.

535
00:42:04,255 --> 00:42:05,422
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

536
00:42:08,592 --> 00:42:09,727
Stop.

537
00:42:10,895 --> 00:42:12,429
- You're here.
- Daimon,

538
00:42:12,496 --> 00:42:14,498
go to Professor Kazama's
operating room now.

539
00:42:15,165 --> 00:42:16,200
What happened?

540
00:42:17,034 --> 00:42:17,868
Hurry.

541
00:42:23,841 --> 00:42:25,042
Daimon.

542
00:42:25,943 --> 00:42:26,977
What about him?

543
00:42:28,512 --> 00:42:33,150
President, are you going to
have Daimon use the robot?

544
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:37,288
Dr. Futaba is the only one
who can use that robot.

545
00:42:38,188 --> 00:42:40,457
Impossible. There's no way she can do it.

546
00:42:40,524 --> 00:42:44,361
Dr. Dangozaka is right.
That woman isn't a brain surgeon.

547
00:42:44,428 --> 00:42:48,098
She's a part-time surgeon.
She'll definitely fail.

548
00:42:50,367 --> 00:42:52,469
- She's coming.
- President.

549
00:43:07,651 --> 00:43:12,256
Can you do it, Dr. Daimon? This surgery.

550
00:43:14,525 --> 00:43:16,927
I don't make mistakes.

551
00:43:23,167 --> 00:43:24,468
Switch patients.

552
00:43:25,035 --> 00:43:26,070
What?

553
00:43:28,772 --> 00:43:30,207
- Switch?
- Switch?

554
00:43:30,274 --> 00:43:32,276
- Switch?
- Did she say to switch patients?

555
00:43:54,965 --> 00:43:55,933
Switch?

556
00:44:09,113 --> 00:44:12,716
- Bleeding stopped.
- Roger. Stopping dopamine.

557
00:44:13,217 --> 00:44:16,387
We'll now begin neuroendoscopic
craniopharyngioma removal.

558
00:44:16,453 --> 00:44:18,322
First, tumor separation.

559
00:44:19,156 --> 00:44:21,191
You're going to do it without the robot?

560
00:44:21,692 --> 00:44:23,994
Daimon, is that really possible?

561
00:44:25,262 --> 00:44:26,397
Answer me.

562
00:44:28,532 --> 00:44:29,366
Biopsy next.

563
00:44:50,587 --> 00:44:51,622
Specimen.

564
00:44:51,689 --> 00:44:52,523
Yes.

565
00:44:53,657 --> 00:44:54,591
She's fast.

566
00:45:13,610 --> 00:45:18,148
Get this tested.
I'll close the incision now.

567
00:45:18,582 --> 00:45:19,717
Get a 0-4 ready too.

568
00:45:19,783 --> 00:45:20,617
Yes.

569
00:45:21,218 --> 00:45:26,223
- Without the robot? Unbelievable.
- Daimon of the east sure is great.

570
00:45:26,690 --> 00:45:30,127
- Fast, cheap, and good.
- What do you mean cheap?

571
00:45:30,661 --> 00:45:32,463
She's cheaper than the robot.

572
00:45:43,240 --> 00:45:45,743
- Sutures complete.
- Thank you.

573
00:45:55,018 --> 00:45:57,287
- Good job.
- See you.

574
00:46:03,093 --> 00:46:06,396
A part-timer saved
the world's greatest brain.

575
00:46:06,463 --> 00:46:07,498
Bravo.

576
00:46:11,668 --> 00:46:12,870
President Tendo.

577
00:46:20,043 --> 00:46:20,878
Thank you.

578
00:46:25,482 --> 00:46:27,918
- MEP waves?
- No problems.

579
00:46:33,123 --> 00:46:34,358
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

580
00:46:50,407 --> 00:46:54,044
- Approaching the midbrain.
- This is the hard part.

581
00:46:55,145 --> 00:46:57,514
If an incision over 5mm
is made in the midbrain,

582
00:46:57,581 --> 00:46:59,049
pyramidal tract will be damaged.

583
00:47:05,823 --> 00:47:10,093
- I hope it'll go well.
- Futaba. Make up for your mistake.

584
00:47:10,994 --> 00:47:13,797
- You can still redeem yourself.
- Yes.

585
00:47:20,504 --> 00:47:22,673
- Sweat.
- Excuse me.

586
00:47:35,686 --> 00:47:37,187
What did she come here for?

587
00:47:37,855 --> 00:47:41,992
You're done over there?
You're fast as usual.

588
00:47:46,530 --> 00:47:49,499
- No, to the right.
- Don't order me.

589
00:47:49,900 --> 00:47:50,834
Diagonally down.

590
00:47:51,835 --> 00:47:54,805
Yes, that's good. Keep going further.

591
00:47:54,872 --> 00:47:59,877
- I said don't order me.
- Right. Cut the arachnoid there.

592
00:47:59,943 --> 00:48:01,778
Shut up. Stop ordering me.

593
00:48:05,749 --> 00:48:08,852
There. Cut the lateral side
of the midbrain vertically.

594
00:48:09,553 --> 00:48:11,288
- Alright.
- Slowly and carefully.

595
00:48:11,355 --> 00:48:12,556
Carefully.

596
00:48:14,524 --> 00:48:17,794
Next. Internal decompression of the tumor.

597
00:48:20,564 --> 00:48:21,465
Change the forceps.

598
00:48:22,866 --> 00:48:23,834
Yes.

599
00:48:24,568 --> 00:48:28,839
Left. The oculomotor nerve
is there so be careful.

600
00:48:31,375 --> 00:48:33,677
Which one is doing the surgery?

601
00:48:35,979 --> 00:48:36,980
Right there.

602
00:48:38,315 --> 00:48:42,653
Separate the tumor and remove it.

603
00:48:59,236 --> 00:49:01,705
The brain stem glioma has been removed.

604
00:49:02,739 --> 00:49:04,141
Get that tested.

605
00:49:04,207 --> 00:49:05,042
Yes.

606
00:49:09,713 --> 00:49:10,647
Irrigation.

607
00:49:14,151 --> 00:49:14,985
Please.

608
00:49:26,930 --> 00:49:27,798
Complete.

609
00:49:29,333 --> 00:49:34,838
Blood loss is 30cc. Blood pressure
in the 100s. Pulse is 80s and sinus.

610
00:49:36,406 --> 00:49:42,245
Well done, Futaba. The world's
first case report using the EX-5.

611
00:49:42,612 --> 00:49:43,747
Bravo.

612
00:49:44,915 --> 00:49:50,387
- Daimon did all of that.
- We did. Our Futaba did it.

613
00:49:53,490 --> 00:49:56,259
- Good job.
- Thank you.

614
00:50:02,499 --> 00:50:04,534
I'll be waiting for good tuna.

615
00:50:09,639 --> 00:50:10,474
Not bad.

616
00:50:12,709 --> 00:50:14,211
- Thanks.
- The robot.

617
00:50:18,548 --> 00:50:20,450
How angering.

618
00:50:33,597 --> 00:50:37,801
The world's No. 1 robot
saved the world's No. 1 dad.

619
00:50:39,236 --> 00:50:41,038
Hey, Ms. Assistant That Got Fired.

620
00:50:44,674 --> 00:50:47,744
I'll tell you the trick
to get the stuffed tuna doll.

621
00:50:50,480 --> 00:50:52,582
No thanks.

622
00:51:00,824 --> 00:51:01,892
That was great.

623
00:51:02,459 --> 00:51:05,629
No one can control
the robot better than you.

624
00:51:05,695 --> 00:51:08,331
Hey, the wizard of laparoscopy
is speaking highly of me.

625
00:51:10,600 --> 00:51:13,970
But today's surgery was Dr. Daimon.

626
00:51:14,671 --> 00:51:17,541
I just did exactly what she told me to do.

627
00:51:19,109 --> 00:51:21,845
That woman learns
people's techniques that way.

628
00:51:21,912 --> 00:51:23,113
She's done it on me often.

629
00:51:24,247 --> 00:51:27,184
The robot memorized
the movements Dr. Daimon ordered.

630
00:51:29,352 --> 00:51:33,256
One day, robots will accurately
duplicate the surgeon's procedures.

631
00:51:33,690 --> 00:51:34,758
Such a day.

632
00:51:39,329 --> 00:51:41,264
Such a day might come one day.

633
00:51:45,402 --> 00:51:47,471
But I'll take the credit.

634
00:51:48,605 --> 00:51:51,308
I'll write a great case report.

635
00:51:52,809 --> 00:51:54,411
Medical science isn't that easy.

636
00:51:58,882 --> 00:52:05,489
Unfortunately, there'll be no case report.

637
00:52:07,224 --> 00:52:09,759
Why is that? Two patients were saved.

638
00:52:09,826 --> 00:52:13,864
Exactly. Both should be
the world's first case.

639
00:52:14,364 --> 00:52:18,869
The case report I wanted,
was a case of the world's

640
00:52:18,935 --> 00:52:21,838
best surgery robot EX-5

641
00:52:22,339 --> 00:52:26,143
saving the brain
of a Nobel Prize prospect.

642
00:52:27,878 --> 00:52:32,082
Otherwise, it doesn't leave
much of an impression.

643
00:52:34,551 --> 00:52:41,324
Also, this was handed in
by Dr. Futaba earlier.

644
00:52:42,526 --> 00:52:45,328
LETTER OF RESIGNATION KENJI FUTABA

645
00:52:45,395 --> 00:52:46,863
Why Dr. Futaba?

646
00:52:48,398 --> 00:52:50,200
Perhaps he's taking responsibility

647
00:52:50,867 --> 00:52:55,372
for making a mistake
in Prof. Kazama's surgery.

648
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:21,331
I don't need people
who let opportunities go to waste.

649
00:53:25,902 --> 00:53:26,836
Hello.

650
00:53:29,172 --> 00:53:34,177
Thank you very much
for using our Daimon and Jonouchi.

651
00:53:35,912 --> 00:53:36,746
This is a melon.

652
00:53:38,682 --> 00:53:39,816
This is a bill.

653
00:53:43,220 --> 00:53:49,326
Excuse me. That's too expensive.
The robot is much cheaper than this.

654
00:53:49,960 --> 00:53:52,395
If you think about the funds
from the government,

655
00:53:52,462 --> 00:53:54,464
it's something as little as a tip.

656
00:53:54,531 --> 00:53:56,266
I don't have a problem with the price.

657
00:53:58,602 --> 00:54:00,670
Please tell Dr. Daimon.

658
00:54:01,204 --> 00:54:03,540
Your skills were excellent,
as the skills of God

659
00:54:03,607 --> 00:54:08,812
that let one get
a taste of the near future.

660
00:54:15,986 --> 00:54:17,420
Thank you.

661
00:54:42,812 --> 00:54:43,947
Damn.

662
00:54:46,583 --> 00:54:49,452
Dad. Are you doing your physical therapy?

663
00:54:49,519 --> 00:54:51,121
Yes. It's pretty hard.

664
00:54:51,187 --> 00:54:54,324
You want to try too, Kazuya?
Here, try holding it.

665
00:55:00,230 --> 00:55:01,064
You okay?

666
00:55:01,665 --> 00:55:02,499
Can you grab it?

667
00:55:06,102 --> 00:55:09,939
I have great news for you board members.

668
00:55:11,908 --> 00:55:15,712
Did you get another
world's first case report?

669
00:55:15,779 --> 00:55:19,816
No. This time,
we got something even more valuable.

670
00:55:22,085 --> 00:55:25,989
Prof. Kazama will be
moving research headquarters

671
00:55:26,389 --> 00:55:29,826
from Harvard to Japan.

672
00:55:34,331 --> 00:55:38,768
My brain was saved by Japan's
state-of-the-art medical science.

673
00:55:39,869 --> 00:55:42,972
It's the least I could do
for President Tendo.

674
00:55:44,574 --> 00:55:50,680
Further research by Prof. Kazama
will all be coming from Japan.

675
00:55:50,747 --> 00:55:56,219
I see. The world's greatest mind
has come back to Japan.

676
00:55:56,286 --> 00:55:57,287
Indeed.

677
00:55:58,221 --> 00:56:00,590
Not only in medical science and physics,

678
00:56:00,657 --> 00:56:03,159
but the brilliant minds in Japan
will be the core of

679
00:56:03,526 --> 00:56:07,630
what leads this nation to become
the leader of the world.

680
00:56:08,498 --> 00:56:13,870
- I truly believe that.
- What a wonderful thought.

681
00:56:14,237 --> 00:56:20,009
- Very well done, President Tendo.
- Absolutely reassuring.

682
00:56:24,914 --> 00:56:26,983
President Tendo,
I'm going to be leaving now.

683
00:56:27,050 --> 00:56:32,021
- We've just begun.
- Are there not enough drinks?

684
00:56:32,088 --> 00:56:37,060
No. There's a sushi restaurant in
Tsukiji that won 3 Michelin stars.

685
00:56:37,660 --> 00:56:39,529
I wanted to take my assistants there.

686
00:56:39,596 --> 00:56:42,432
I see. That's a great idea.

687
00:56:45,935 --> 00:56:46,770
Well then.

688
00:56:50,206 --> 00:56:54,411
For humanity's... No. For Japan's future.

689
00:56:57,647 --> 00:57:01,684
Alright. I was able to grab it.

690
00:57:03,486 --> 00:57:07,857
I honestly didn't think
I'd be able to eat your sushi again.

691
00:57:08,358 --> 00:57:10,293
Are you doing your physical therapy?

692
00:57:10,360 --> 00:57:13,163
Making sushi is the best therapy.

693
00:57:13,229 --> 00:57:17,367
If you say my sushi isn't packed
tightly again, I'll be very angry.

694
00:57:17,434 --> 00:57:20,603
Then let's have you do lots of therapy.

695
00:57:20,670 --> 00:57:25,909
Yeah. Here I go.
Rosy seabass, tuna, and tuna.

696
00:57:25,975 --> 00:57:29,512
Gizzard shad, flounder,
filefish, rosy seabass, tuna.

697
00:57:29,579 --> 00:57:32,348
<i>She despises teams, authority</i>
<i>and the restraints they bring.</i>

698
00:57:32,415 --> 00:57:36,619
<i>Her license and the skills</i>
<i>she has earned are her only weapons.</i>

699
00:57:48,998 --> 00:57:50,166
This is the place.

700
00:57:51,968 --> 00:57:53,002
You idiot.

701
00:57:54,070 --> 00:57:57,440
How many times did I tell you
not to put soy sauce on that?

702
00:57:57,507 --> 00:58:03,246
- You're ruining the fish.
- I'll eat it how I want to.

703
00:58:03,313 --> 00:58:06,216
You didn't listen to me,
so I won't listen to you.

704
00:58:12,755 --> 00:58:16,593
You shouldn't be coming here
if you don't understand good sushi.

705
00:58:16,926 --> 00:58:18,728
Get out of here.

706
00:58:25,235 --> 00:58:26,102
Let's go home.

707
00:58:26,569 --> 00:58:29,672
Prof. Kazama, the 3-star restaurant
seems to be over there.

708
00:58:34,210 --> 00:58:38,648
Stop complaining and make me some tuna.

709
00:58:38,715 --> 00:58:41,818
What did you say?
You're like a hungry brat.

710
00:58:41,885 --> 00:58:45,221
- Tuna.
- Can't you be more ladylike?

711
00:58:45,288 --> 00:58:50,960
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

712
01:00:09,439 --> 01:00:11,641
The president of
the Nurse's Federation is here.

713
01:00:11,708 --> 01:00:14,811
- Too much skin.
- That hurts.

714
01:00:14,877 --> 01:00:18,147
If a doctor makes an enemy out of
shogun's harem, their career is over.

715
01:00:18,615 --> 01:00:20,950
- Wall slam.
- Don't even think about it.

716
01:00:21,017 --> 01:00:23,953
Forget about scheming
when there's a life on the line.
